## Context

The wizard + canvas editor UI has been redesigned with the TrueKeeps Design System and looks production-quality, but exploration confirms the app is currently a **front-end prototype**: photos are stored as base64 strings in memory, there is no auth, no real checkout (the button fires a toast), no print-ready export, no image processing, and the "AI auto-layout" is a hardcoded grid. This document is (1) a product/UX gap analysis with an AI strategy, and (2) the FE/BE/infra architecture to take it from prototype → sellable product at 100 → 1k → 10k users, followed by a phased build roadmap.

