# Build roadmap (when we implement)

- **Phase 0 — Truthful UI + updated design (2–3 days):** wire or remove dead controls in `create.tsx` (sliders, layout buttons, Save, 3D preview, "of 20"); remove emoji; apply Step-3 layout choice to page generation. Port the updated landing composition from `~/Downloads/landing.jsx` into `client/src/pages/home.tsx` (TrustStrip/HowItWorks/Showcase/Occasions/Proof/FinalCTA sections, scroll-reveal as a `useScrollReveal` hook) and restructure the wizard to the quiz-first flow from `~/Downloads/app.jsx` (quiz screen with occasion/vibe → upload → generating → reveal → preview, "Customize" branch into the canvas editor), converted to typed TSX with the state machine in `wizard-types.ts`.
- **Phase 1 — Real persistence & media (core):** enable Postgres in `server/storage.ts`; R2 presigned uploads; client compression worker; `sharp` thumbnail job via pg-boss; HEIC + EXIF handling. Files: `server/storage.ts`, `server/routes.ts`, new `server/media.ts`, `server/queue.ts`, `client/src/components/wizard/PhotoUpload.tsx`.
- **Phase 2 — Commerce:** sessions + guest auth, `orders` schema, payment provider interface (gateway TBD with user), order status page, confirmation + draft-recovery emails.
- **Phase 3 — Print pipeline:** puppeteer render job → print PDF in R2 → manual printer handoff; preflight warnings in PageReview.
- **Phase 4 — AI:** dedup/quality scoring → EXIF chaptering → aspect-aware layouts → Claude Haiku captions (port occasion/caption model from design system's `book_builder/data.jsx`).

## Verification
- Each phase: `npm run check` (0 TS errors) + `npm run dev` on :5001 and drive the full wizard end-to-end with real photos (incl. one HEIC, one 20MB image).
- Phase 1: restart server mid-draft → draft survives; check R2 objects + thumbnails exist.
- Phase 2: test-mode payment → order row + email + status page.
- Phase 3: open generated PDF, verify DPI/bleed at physical size.
